From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] synth: SKIP_EXTRACT_FA, a turnaround knob for arithmetic-heavy
 modules

extract_fa runs unconditionally before the adder techmap. On
arithmetic-heavy modules it is the largest share of the partition's
time: in XiangShan's vector converter 83% (748 s) and in a vector FMA
51% (848 s) of the synthesis, ahead of abc. SKIP_EXTRACT_FA=1 leaves the
adders to the generic techmap, which is what architectural exploration
wants while the flow is being put together; the default is unchanged.

Not upstreamed; carried by bazel-orfs. Retires at a //:bump onto an ORFS
that carries a knob for this.
---
diff --git a/flow/scripts/synth.tcl b/flow/scripts/synth.tcl
--- a/flow/scripts/synth.tcl
+++ b/flow/scripts/synth.tcl
@@ -240,7 +240,9 @@
   )
 } {
   # extract the full adders
-  extract_fa
+  if { ![env_var_equals SKIP_EXTRACT_FA 1] } {
+    extract_fa
+  }
   # map full adders
   techmap -map $::env(ADDER_MAP_FILE)
   techmap
diff --git a/flow/scripts/variables.yaml b/flow/scripts/variables.yaml
--- a/flow/scripts/variables.yaml
+++ b/flow/scripts/variables.yaml
@@ -885,6 +885,17 @@
     - cts
     - floorplan
     - grt
+SKIP_EXTRACT_FA:
+  description: >
+    Skip yosys's extract_fa before the adder techmap. Full-adder
+    extraction is a large share of synthesis time on arithmetic-heavy
+    modules (an FMA or a vector converter can spend most of its
+    partition in it); without it adders map through the generic techmap.
+    A turnaround setting for architectural exploration.
+  stages:
+    - synth
+  default: 0
+
 SKIP_CTS_REPAIR_TIMING:
   description: >
     Skipping CTS repair, which can take a long time, can be useful in
